  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Psalms",
    "delineation": "Psalm",
    "number": 59,
    "summary": "David prays to be delivered from his enemies—God rules in Jacob unto the ends of the earth.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Deliver me from mine enemies, O my God: defend me from them that rise up against me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 59:1",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 59,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Deliver me from the workers of iniquity, and save me from bloody men.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 7,
            "text": "D&C 10:5."
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 64,
            "text": "OR bloodthirsty."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "D&C 10:5.",
            "prettyString": "D&C 10:5",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "doctrineandcovenants",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 10,
                    "end": 10,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 5,
                        "end": 5
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 59:2",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 59,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "For, lo, they lie in wait for my soul: the mighty are gathered against me; not for my transgression, nor for my sin, O Lord.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 79,
            "end": 82
          },
          {
            "start": 105,
            "end": 108
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 59:3",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 59,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "They run and prepare themselves without my fault: awake to help me, and behold.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "OR for no guilt of mine."
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "Ps. 35:23."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 42
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Ps. 35:23.",
            "prettyString": "Psalms 35:23",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "psalms",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 35,
                    "end": 35,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 23,
                        "end": 23
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 59:4",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 59,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Thou therefore, O Lord God of hosts, the God of Israel, awake to visit all the heathen: be not merciful to any wicked transgressors. Selah.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 59:5",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 59,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "They return at evening: they make a noise like a dog, and go round about the city.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 59:6",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 59,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, they belch out with their mouth: swords are in their lips: for who, say they, doth hear?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 47,
            "text": "Ps. 57:4."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 51
          },
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 85
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Ps. 57:4.",
            "prettyString": "Psalms 57:4",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "psalms",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 57,
                    "end": 57,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 4,
                        "end": 4
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 59:7",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 59,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "But thou, O Lord, shalt laugh at them; thou shalt have all the heathen in derision.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 59:8",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 59,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Because of his strength will I wait upon thee: for God is my defence.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 10
          },
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 57
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 59:9",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 59,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "The God of my mercy shall prevent me: God shall let me see my desire upon mine enemies.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3,
            "text": "HEB My God, in His loving kindness, shall go before me."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 68
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 59:10",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 59,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Slay them not, lest my people forget: scatter them by thy power; and bring them down, O Lord our shield.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 59:11",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 59,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "For the sin of their mouth and the words of their lips let them even be taken in their pride: and for cursing and lying which they speak.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3
          },
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 30
          },
          {
            "start": 120,
            "end": 125
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 59:12",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 59,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "Consume them in wrath, consume them, that they may not be: and let them know that God ruleth in Jacob unto the ends of the earth. Selah.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 12
          },
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 36
          },
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 50
          },
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 58
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 59:13",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 59,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "And at evening let them return; and let them make a noise like a dog, and go round about the city.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 35
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 59:14",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 59,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "Let them wander up and down for meat, and grudge if they be not satisfied.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 59:15",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 59,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "But I will sing of thy power; yea, I will sing aloud of thy mercy in the morning: for thou hast been my defence and refuge in the day of my trouble.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 140,
            "end": 147,
            "text": "TG Adversity."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Adversity.",
            "prettyString": "TG Adversity",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Adversity",
                "entryId": "tg-adversity",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 59:16",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 59,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "Unto thee, O my strength, will I sing: for God is my defence, and the God of my mercy.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 49
          },
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 65
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 59:17",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 59,
        "verse": 17
      }
    ]
  },
